B. Degree-two branch on explicit sphere models
  exchange: commute fails 0, f.iota=tau.f fails 0, (tau u=u) != (delta s=iota s) 0, axis collapses 2000
    ramification 1: branch value (2+0j), tau-fixed True
    ramification -1: branch value (-2+0j), tau-fixed True
  preserve: commute fails 0, f.iota=tau.f fails 0, (tau u=u) != (delta s=iota s) 0, axis collapses 0
    ramification 0: branch value 0j, tau-fixed n/a (0 <-> inf)
  preserve: branch values 0 and inf are swapped by tau(u)=1/conj(u),
  so they form the unique nonreal (off-seam) branch pair.

C. Axis lemma: winding of gamma * reflect(gamma)^-1 about p on the axis
  loops with odd winding: 500/500
  Odd winding means the loop encloses p, so a simply connected
  symmetric room has no gap point: the axis meets it in one interval.
